From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:50:33 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: quiesce TX and defer country updates across
 suspend

Cache regulatory requests under RTNL while the wiphy is suspended and
replay the latest valid country from wiphy resume, after transport
resume. Keep failed updates pending and preserve the initial band
setup until it succeeds.

Stop and drain network TX before the PCIe D3 handshake, fence
message-buffer TX and flowring workers while retaining their
pending work, and restart them only after interrupts and HOSTREADY
are restored. Track bus flow control independently so resume cannot
clear disconnected or firmware flow-control stops. Restore the console
timer and TX on a failed D3 handshake.

Add production-code host controls for regulatory replay, TX stop
reasons, deferred workers, retained/cold resume and suspend rollback,
with five assertion-producing mutations.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>

(backported from commit 43d03538d381d35a414badc99035f7a86b823747)
[j604: dropped the tools/asahi/run-host-tests.py hunk that registers the new host test; the 1.607 base
 has no run-host-tests.py (Aurora added the runner later). Kernel code identical to upstream; the test file is kept
 and runs standalone with python3 -I.]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
